    "result_text": "There's exactly one test class and it passes. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI updated `OwnerCreationAuditor.auditOwnerCreated` to emit an immutable structured `OWNER_CREATED` event via the dedicated `AUDIT` logger, in addition to the existing human-readable audit line.\n\n**File changed:** `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerCreationAuditor.java`\n\nThe new event is a single-line JSON object built with Jackson:\n```\n{\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"customerCode\":\"NSW-16E6609E\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}\n```\n\nKey design points matching the spec:\n\n- **`seq`** \u2014 a `static final AtomicLong` incremented on every create, so it's monotonically increasing across all owner creations (process-wide).\n- **`ownerId`**, **`membershipLevel`**, **`event:'OWNER_CREATED'`** \u2014 as specified.\n- **Primary identifier abstraction** \u2014 the `customerCode` value is sourced through a small private `primaryIdentifier(Owner)` seam rather than read inline. It returns `owner.getCustomerCode()` today; when the customer code is later unified into the member id, that single method changes and the event automatically carries the member id instead \u2014 exactly the future evolution the spec calls out.\n- The event is immutable \u2014 it's constructed fresh, serialized to a string, and logged; nothing holds a mutable reference.\n\nThe acceptance test (`AcceptanceTest.coreEventCarriesIdAndIdentifier`) and the full suite pass \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.",
